From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:18:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: show every pull request of an agent and react to their
 reviews and CI

The composer showed one change request: the one of the branch checked out
in the workspace. An agent that opens several, or that hands work to
subagents in other worktrees, had the rest out of sight, and every review,
failed check or conflict needed someone to notice it and click a follow-up.

The daemon now tracks the change requests each agent works on: the one of
the branch checked out where it runs, and every one a tool call of its own
created (gh pr create and the like, or an MCP create tool). Links are saved
in $PASEO_HOME/agent-pull-requests.json, because a finished subagent's
timeline is not loaded again. agent.pull_requests.list returns them for an
agent and all of its subagents, and the app shows one pill per change
request, with the follow-ups of each.

The daemon also listens to those change requests. Every 90 seconds it
reads the open ones and sends the quick action prompt for a new conflict,
a failed head commit or a new review to one agent per change request, once
that agent is idle. It is on for every session unless the agent carries
the label paseo.pr-auto-listen=off, which the app's new checkbox pill sets
through the existing update_agent_request. The first look after a start
only notes what is there, Fix CI stops after three failed heads in a row,
and review comments posted during the agent's own turn count as its
replies, so it never answers itself.

The follow-ups are the quick actions: a new Address review action joins
them, and the app sends its prompts (the customized ones included) to the
host with agent.pull_requests.set_prompts.

Nothing changes for other clients on the wire: two request/response pairs
they never send, two optional server_info.features flags
(agentPullRequests, pullRequestAutoListen) and one agent label.

